# Entes MPR-3X / MPR-4X.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Entes MPR-3X / MPR-4X series — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: Entes "MPR 3X-4X Register table" (Measurements block @ 0, Energy @ 200).
# | - Mixed types: voltages/currents/frequency are UINT32 (2 registers), powers are
# | IEEE-754 FLOAT (f32), power factor / CosPhi are INT32, energy counters are
# | UINT64 (4 registers). All Big-Endian (most-significant word first) — the
# | default — so `word_order` is omitted. (Verify on your unit; if values look
# | byte-swapped, add `word_order = "le"`.)
# | - Manual scale folded into `scale`:  V x0.1 -> 0.1   A x0.001 -> 0.001
# | Hz x0.01 -> 0.01   PF/CosPhi x0.001 -> 0.001   power & energy raw (scale 1).
# | - Addresses are the protocol addresses, in decimal (0x0000 = 0).
# | - Factory defaults: device address (slave) = 1, RTU = 9600 baud (check unit).
# | 
# | Workspace fields below activate in Phase 1 (currently ignored by the build):
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Entes
@model=MPR-3X / MPR-4X
@description=3-/4-phase power analyser — V/I/P/Q/S per phase and total, power factor, CosPhi, frequency and 64-bit energy meters.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/entes-mpr-3x-4x.toml; Source: Entes "MPR 3X-4X Register table" (Measurements block @ 0, Energy @ 200).. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

